{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>There is one who speaks rashly</b> — the matter is connected to what precedes, with 'false witness.' That is, there is one who speaks rashly and expounds false testimony, and the testimony is piercing like the thrusts of a sword." "<b>And the tongue of the wise</b> — they are the investigators of the testimony and refute the one thrust, namely the false witness. Another interpretation: 'there is one who speaks rashly' on account of the one who vows a harsh thing. n: 'the one who vows' (הנודר) is unclear in context; translated literally."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:24.079448932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}